      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Solid-state SQUID data for the 4f7 Eu(II) trimer show χMT = 24.5 emu K mol−1 at 297 K (vs 23.6 calculated for three isolated Eu(II) ions). χMT is constant from 300–60 K then rises to a maximum of 32.9 emu K mol−1 at 6 K, indicating weak ferromagnetic coupling (best fit J = 0.1035 cm−1, g = 2.0281). X-band EPR of the ground solid at 10 K shows a single feature at geff = 2.1.",
