        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A cold (−40 °C) THF solution of (Ph2SiOK)2O (41.6 mg, 0.085 mmol, 3 equiv; 1 mL) was added to a stirring orange suspension of 1-Eu3L3 (58.1 mg, 0.028 mmol, 1 equiv) in THF (0.5 mL) at −40 °C. The orange solution was stirred 30 min at −40 °C. Volatiles were removed, the yellow residue was suspended in Et2O (8 mL), and the orange slurry was filtered. Concentration of the filtrate (~1 mL) and storage at −40 °C overnight yielded orange crystals (56%, 50.6 mg, 0.012 mmol). Dark yellow XRD crystals were obtained by slow diffusion of n-hexane into an Et2O solution at −40 °C.",
